status :

what can it parse, where does it fails ?

why is there a alabnf - albnf_test.c) and alabanf_matcher ?

alabnf.c => read/parse a stream of ABNF syntax and create and struct abnf* internal represention of it

alabnf_test.c is used for alabnf main and does only parse ABNF to validate it is a correct ABNF syntax

alabnf infile=<file to parse>



alabnf_matcher_test is main for alabnf_matcher

alabnf_matcher <number of > <abnf file>+

list of ABNF syntax to build one parser then apply it on stdin

